From ebeb04ef56cc5f4b0a6949990ab31fa8972e25fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:24:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] G31A-TIME: golden's automatic motor power-on fires on
 golden's time (100 calls or 1 s), not after ~100 s of 500 ms ticks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930, after dcc1323: "還是一樣的狀況 我都需要先放激磁 再開 機構才可以移動".
Measured oplog_20260930.txt, run 09:17:01 (exe built 09:16:49, i.e. with dcc1323):
  09:17:11     BrakeAxisTick releases MOutArmZA / MLoaderZ / MAuto1Z (SVON carried over)
  09:17:53     Motor Test FormShow -> DoMotorPowerOn: TMySwitch::Status() reads the relay's OutPortData (0, never commanded
               this run) although the card reads it ON -> relay On + CassetteBreakerOFF() -> brakes held
  09:18:21     operator servo off: "it was already held"; servo on -> released
  09:18:55     PAGE power 0->1 -- bMotorPowerState, i.e. golden G31a, ~114 s after START
  09:18:57     dcc1323's per-axis release runs for the first time (MOutArmZA, MLoaderZ) -- W906_BrakeReleaseOK refuses every
               group while bMotorPowerState is false, so it could not act earlier
Cause: CheckMotorPowerShutDown's `DelayMotNo>=100` counts calls, one per 2 DoSystem passes. golden's MainProc runs at ~1 ms
(B13), so golden powers on a fraction of a second after start-up and the operator never meets this window; on wb_serve's
500 ms tick (B13, deliberate, unchanged) it is ~100 s.
Fix (csystem.cpp CheckMotorPowerShutDown): `flag && (DelayMotNo>=100 || 1 s since the first counted call)`. Same golden body,
same EastSun ruling 20260926 on G31a ("照舊版打開"); only its timing is restored. After it, Motor Test FormShow finds the relay
already commanded (no second DoMotorPowerOn hold), and the golden releases (G16 / G05, per axis since dcc1323) are allowed.
Built wb_serve in build_integ_ship_x86_o2. Not run on the machine yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 csystem.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/csystem.cpp b/csystem.cpp
index f23e5d8..e650995 100644
--- a/csystem.cpp
+++ b/csystem.cpp
@@ -16060,7 +16060,22 @@ void CheckMotorPowerShutDown()
 
         if(IsSafeLockCheck())
             return ;
-        if(flag && DelayMotNo>=100)
+//AI(W906-G31A-TIME) 20260930: EastSun「還是一樣的狀況 我都需要先放激磁 再開 機構才可以移動」. golden's 100 is a count of
+//  CheckMotorPowerShutDown calls = 200 DoSystem passes (it runs only when bDoProcess, which flips every pass) on golden's
+//  ~1 ms MainProc (TRunControl, timeBeginPeriod(1); docs/RULINGS_20260917.md B13) -- i.e. golden's automatic motor
+//  power-on happens a fraction of a second after start-up. On wb_serve's 500 ms tick (B13, deliberate) the same 100 calls
+//  take ~100 s: measured oplog_20260930.txt, START 09:17:01 -> PAGE power 0->1 at 09:18:55. Until then bMotorPowerState is
+//  false, so every golden brake release (W906_BrakeReleaseOK) is refused, and the Motor Test FormShow of that window
+//  (09:17:53) runs DoMotorPowerOn with the relay's OutPortData still 0 (TMySwitch::Status() reads the command cache, not
+//  the card) -> CassetteBreakerOFF() -> the Loader / Auto1 brakes held for the rest of those ~100 s; the operator's
+//  servo off/on (a fresh SVON edge for BrakeAxisTick) was the only way out. golden's operator never sees that window.
+//  So the threshold is golden's TIME, not its pass count: 100 calls OR 1 s since the first counted call, whichever first
+//  (1 s = one CheckMotorPowerShutDown call on this tick; golden's own delay is shorter still). Same golden body below,
+//  EastSun ruling 20260926 "照舊版打開" on G31a unchanged -- this only restores its timing.
+        static DWORD W906_G31aFirstMs=0;
+        if(W906_G31aFirstMs==0)
+            W906_G31aFirstMs=::GetTickCount()|1u;
+        if(flag && (DelayMotNo>=100 || (::GetTickCount()-W906_G31aFirstMs)>=1000u))
         {
 //AI(ht9045-v906) 20260810: PT-W5c audit finding 4 -- THE ORIGINAL REASON BELOW WAS FALSE,
 // AND THE GATE IS STILL CORRECT. Corrected reason first, original text kept after it:
-- 
2.55.0.windows.5

